@DATABASE PhoenixCfg.Guide
@INDEX Index

@NODE main "PhoenixCfg help guide"
@NEXT MainWnd
@TOC main
Welcome to PhoenixCfg help Guide.

   @{" Main window    " Link MainWnd}
   @{" Paths window   " Link PathsWnd}
   @{" Door Id window " Link DoorIdWnd}

PhoenixCfg tries to save the window's positions on exit. You can avoid
this by using the "NoXy" argument, either at CLI or as an icon
tooltype.

Note: The index doesn't do anything yet.
@ENDNODE

:###############
;# MAIN WINDOW #
;###############
@NODE MainWnd
@PREV main
@NEXT PathsWnd
@{b}BBS Id:@{ub}
A unique identification string for your BBS' mail packets. The string can
be upto 6 characters long (Because of Phoenix ability to store several
packets for a user). E.g. our BBS' name is CeCom and the BBS Id is CeCom.

@{b}Phone no:@{ub}
Telephone number to your BBS.

@{b}Primary address:@{ub}
Your primary network address. E.g. mine is "39:22/1.0" (AmigaNet).
You only have to fill in this if you're in a FidoNet compatible network.

@{b}Msgs packet:@{ub}
Max number of messages in a mail packet. This overrides any limit the
user might choose. I.e. if you enter 1000 and the user 2000, 1000 will
be used.

@{b}Msgs area:@{ub}
Max number of messages in a mail packet. This overrides any limit the
user might choose. I.e. if you enter 300 and the user 500, 300 will
be used.

@{b}Memory usage:@{ub}
The size of the buffer that's used when scanning messages. Beware: This
is not kilobytes. If you choose "Other" you can enter the size of the
buffer in the integer gadget to the right. Figures below 32 is not
recommended.

@{b}Paths:@{ub}
Open/pop to front the @{"paths" Link PathsWnd} window.

@{b}Door Id:@{ub}
Open/pop to front the @{"Door Id" Link DoorIdWnd} window.
@ENDNODE

;################
;# PATHS WINDOW #
;################
@NODE PathsWnd
@PREV MainWnd
@NEXT DoorIdWnd
@{b}Hello:@{ub}
Full path to a hello/welcome ANSI/ASCII text file. This might be displayed
to the user before he read the messages. Only supported in QwkExport so
far.

@{b}Goodbye:@{ub}
Full path to a goodbye ANSI/ASCII text file. This might be displayed
to the user when he stops reading the messages. Only supported in QwkExport
so far.

@{b}News:@{ub}
Full path to a news letter ANSI/ASCII text file. It should tell about the
latest events/news on your BBS. Only supported in QwkExport so far.

@{b}File list:@{ub}
Full path to a RECENT/new files list. Only supported in QwkExport so far.

@{b}Work:@{ub}
Path to a directory/unit where Phoenix should work. If this is located
on your ram disc grabing etc will be faster, however it could be filled,
so be sure have enough ram.

@{b}BEWARE:@{ub} Everything here, but "Work", is optional. I.e. you MUST fill in
        "Work".
@ENDNODE

;##################
;# DOOR ID WINDOW #
;##################
@NODE DoorIdWnd
@PREV PathsWnd
@NEXT main
With the check marks/flags you can allow/disallow control types. This
makes it possible for the user to change information/setings remotely
by entering a message to the name in "Control name".

E.g. Add: @{b}<area number>@{ub} tells the usage of the control type.

Example control message:
TO     : Phoenix
FROM   : Olav Den Hellige
SUBJECT: Doesn't matter
----------------------------------
ADD 350
RESET 350 1548
DROP 650

@{b}Add:@{ub} <area number>
Join a conference.
E.g. "ADD 26"

@{b}Drop:@{ub} <area number>
Resign a conference.
E.g. "DROP 145"

@{b}Reset:@{ub}

@{b}Bulletins:@{ub}

@{b}File list:@{ub}

@{b}Request:@{ub}

@{b}Index:@{ub}

@{b}News:@{ub}

@{b}Hello:@{ub}

@{b}Goodbye:@{ub}

@{b}Max area:@{ub}

@{b}Max packet:@{ub}

@{b}Password:@{ub}

@{b}Screen height:@{ub} <height>
Sets the screen/page length. If zero more prompts are disabled.
E.g. "PAGELEN 30"

@{b}Screen width:@{ub}
Sets the screen width.
E.g. "PAGEWIDTH 78"

@{b}Expert mode:@{ub}

@{b}Protocol:@{ub}

@{b}Location:@{ub}

@{b}Data phone:@{ub}

@{b}Voice phone:@{ub}

@{b}Help:@{ub}

@{b}Control name:@{ub}
A name, which the user must send control messages to. E.g. "Phoenix".

@{b}Reply area:@{ub}
Which area Phoenix should answer control messages (Tell if it was
successfull). E.g. "Post". This is not supported yet.

@{b}NOTE:@{ub} Control types are only supported in QwkImport for now.
      The control types with no description aren't supported yet.
@ENDNODE

